ly Tang Williams in a rematch for New Hampshire's second congressional district. Recent polls from the University of New Hampshire and Saint Anselm College show Goodlander ahead by 15 to 21 points among likely voters, and she has raised roughly $4.2 million to Williams' $1.2 million. Expert raters uniformly place the race at Likely D or better, with several calling it Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price her win probability around 93 percent.\n\nThe district leans slightly Democratic, and the incumbent's financial and polling advantages point to a comfortable margin. Williams has some name recognition from the previous contest, but no evidence suggests a fundamental shift in the race's trajectory. The forecast expects a double-digit Democratic win with modest residual uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9818, "margin": 13.85}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9772, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.978, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9795, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9872, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.0}]}